course: dictionary
lesson: 12011
title: Cheery
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cheery is an adjective. It describes a person, a voice, a place or a colour, and it means happy and friendly in a bright, lively way. «Mum gave me a cheery wave from the gate.» A wave cannot be happy on its own, so cheery tells you how the wave was done: warmly, with a smile.
explain: Look at the words around cheery to work out its meaning. «The cheery room had yellow walls and sunny curtains.» Walls and curtains cannot feel happy, so cheery here means bright and pleasant to be in.
explain: Cheery often comes before a noun, as in «a cheery hello», «a cheery smile» or «cheery news». To check your meaning, swap in happy: «a happy smile» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Cheery is an adjective: it describes a noun.
fact: «Cheery» means happy and friendly in a bright, lively way.
fact: «Cheery» can also describe things that make you feel happy, like a room or a colour.
fact: Cheerier and cheeriest compare things: «She was cheerier today» and «He was the cheeriest boy in class».
fact: Cheery is close to happy, but it often suggests a lively, friendly feeling you can see or hear.
exercise: «Mum gave me a cheery wave from the gate.» What does cheery mean here? | Lost and worried | Tired and slow | *Happy and friendly | Angry and loud
exercise: «The cheery room had yellow walls and sunny curtains.» What does cheery describe? | *A room that feels bright and pleasant | A window that is broken | A wall that is cold and damp | A dog that is hungry
exercise: Ravi says «cheery» means sad. Who is right? | Neither of them knows the word | Ravi is right, because cheery means sad | Both are right, because they mean the same | *Ravi is wrong, because cheery means happy
test: «She gave a cheery smile when she saw her friend.» What does cheery tell us about the smile? | Heavy and grey | Rude and short | Sleepy and slow | *Bright and happy
test: Which phrase uses cheery to mean a happy greeting? | a cheery storm | *a cheery hello | a cheery mud | a cheery stone
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to cheery? | heavy | angry | quiet | *happy
